 "skipped": [
  "p. 222: footnote 1, a 'less corrupt text' of lines 1–4 printed in hieroglyphs from Naville, Todtenbuch Bd. II, Bl. 332",
  "p. 223: footnotes 1–4, variant spellings (sekertu; 'pigs and donkeys'; 'satisfying the heart of the king and of his nobles'; 'shall be given to him bread, vessels of drink, cakes')",
  "p. 224: the section headed 'Appendix.' (from Naville, Todtenbuch Bd. I, Bl. 140) and its footnote"
 ],
 "layoutNote": "Plate XXXIII lines 1–10 (pp. 222–224). The line numerals 2. and 9. are set inside the words tebtu and setau - tuf; those words carry the line in which they begin (1 and 8). Rubric (overlined in the type): p. 222 row 1 àn and unχ - f … θàb only; p. 222 rows 2–3 and p. 223 rows 1–4 throughout; p. 223 row 5 except suten; p. 223 row 6 and p. 224 not at all.",
 "footnotes": [
  "p. 222 n. 1 (on àn, line 1): A less corrupt text of lines 1–4 reads as follows (See Naville, Todtenbuch, Bd. II., Bl. 332):— [hieroglyphs with transliteration: àrit mà χeper āb[et] ent Maāti t'eṭ se re pen | 2. āb turà unχ - nef ḥebs en ṭept tebu em | 3. ḥet'eti mesṭemu em mesṭemt urḥ em ṭept | ent ānta | 4. uṭen - nef ka uat' apt neter sentrà | tau ḥeqt semu | às àri - nek sem pen em ān; English: To be done as one cometh to the Hall of Maāti. Shall say a man chapter this cleansed, purified. He shall be girt about with garments of the finest quality, shod with white sandals, [the eyes] smeared with eye-paint, anointed with the finest of ānta unguent. Must be offered unto him a bull, vegetables, ducks, incense, cakes, beer, herbs. Behold thou must make picture this in writing, etc.] (OUT of section)",
  "p. 223 n. 1 (on sekertu, line 4): Var. [hieroglyphs: two variant spellings of sekertu, each O34 over a star-like/spindle sign over D21 (or V31), with determinatives; the second ends in a flat roll Y1 over Z2].",
  "p. 223 n. 2 (on the determinative of śaāa, line 5): Var. [hieroglyphs: pig + Z1, donkey + Z1] \"pigs and donkeys.\"",
  "p. 223 n. 3 (on śeni - f, line 7): Var. [hieroglyphs: G17, sickle-like sign over D46/Y1, F34+Z1, N35, M23 X1:N35 + seated king, V28 N35:D36, V7:N35 M17 M17 + seated man + standing figure, Z1, I9] \"satisfying the heart of the king and of his nobles.\"",
  "p. 223 n. 4 (on ṭes, line 7): Var. [hieroglyphs] ṭātu-nef ṣenset ṭes pa-sen, \"shall be given to him bread, vessels of drink, cakes.\""
 ],
